                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A system of cryptography."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f15ec47-5706-450a-85b4-4f0216de4c67",
                                                "sense_id": "4ff4fa7e-ed0f-3cd8-baee-6ce188cf5108",
                                                "text": "In our example of the affine cryptosystem family, deciphering is also accomplished by an affine map, namely P#92;equiva#123;-1#125;C-a#123;-1#125;b#92;bmodN, and so the deciphering transformation uses the same algorithm as the enciphering transformation, except with a different key, namely, the pair (a#123;-1#125;,-a#123;-1#125;b)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "828f27a3-38bd-4abc-b09d-bad86d9034cb",
                                                "sense_id": "4ff4fa7e-ed0f-3cd8-baee-6ce188cf5108",
                                                "text": "Our results show that many existing fast pseudomultiplication implementations (hitherto limited to applications in Diffie--Hellman key exchange) can be wrapped with simple and efficient pre-and post-computations to yield competitive full scalar multiplication algorithms, ready for use in more general discrete logarithm-based cryptosystems, including signature schemes."
                                            }
                                        ]
